{%- liquid
  assign po_product = product.title | url_encode
  capture po_link_raw
    echo shop.url
    echo product.url
  endcapture
  assign po_link = po_link_raw | url_encode
  comment
    Desktop lays three shots out beside the information column, so it needs to
    know which media belong to which colour.

    The variant's own featured_media is the authority: it is Shopify's real
    variant-to-media relationship, and it is what IMG 1 becomes. Position is
    only ever used afterwards, to pick up the shots uploaded alongside it, and
    it can never override a media item another colour's variant points at.
  endcomment
  assign color_option = null
  for product_option in product.options_with_values
    assign option_name = product_option.name | downcase
    if option_name contains 'color' or option_name contains 'colour'
      assign color_option = product_option
      break
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Review data is the product's own, from its metafields. The section's
    settings are only a store-wide sample, used when a product has none and the
    merchant has asked for them -- off by default, so a product without review
    data shows no review section rather than another product's numbers.

    Whatever the source, the count is the sum of the star distribution and the
    average its weighted mean, so the headline, the bars and the summary's
    "based on" line can never disagree.
  endcomment
  assign mf = product.metafields.custom
  assign use_sample = section.settings.reviews_fallback

  comment
    Shopify builds a metafield's key from the name it is given, so a definition
    called "Reviews 5 star" ends up at reviews_5_star rather than reviews_5.
    Both spellings are read, so the definitions work whichever way they were
    created.
  endcomment
  assign r5 = mf.reviews_5.value | default: mf.reviews_5_star.value | default: 0 | times: 1
  assign r4 = mf.reviews_4.value | default: mf.reviews_4_star.value | default: 0 | times: 1
  assign r3 = mf.reviews_3.value | default: mf.reviews_3_star.value | default: 0 | times: 1
  assign r2 = mf.reviews_2.value | default: mf.reviews_2_star.value | default: 0 | times: 1
  assign r1 = mf.reviews_1.value | default: mf.reviews_1_star.value | default: 0 | times: 1
  assign review_total = r5 | plus: r4 | plus: r3 | plus: r2 | plus: r1

  assign review_fit_label = mf.review_fit_label.value
  assign review_fit_position = mf.review_fit_position.value | default: 50 | times: 1
  assign review_summary_text = mf.review_summary.value
  assign review_keywords_text = mf.review_keywords.value

  if review_total == 0 and use_sample
    assign r5 = section.settings.reviews_5 | default: 0 | times: 1
    assign r4 = section.settings.reviews_4 | default: 0 | times: 1
    assign r3 = section.settings.reviews_3 | default: 0 | times: 1
    assign r2 = section.settings.reviews_2 | default: 0 | times: 1
    assign r1 = section.settings.reviews_1 | default: 0 | times: 1
    assign review_total = r5 | plus: r4 | plus: r3 | plus: r2 | plus: r1
    if review_fit_label == blank
      assign review_fit_label = section.settings.fit_label
      assign review_fit_position = section.settings.fit_position | default: 50 | times: 1
    endif
    if review_summary_text == blank
      assign review_summary_text = section.settings.review_summary
    endif
    if review_keywords_text == blank
      assign review_keywords_text = section.settings.review_keywords
    endif
  endif

  assign has_distribution = false
  if review_total > 0
    assign has_distribution = true
    assign weighted = r5 | times: 5
    assign part = r4 | times: 4
    assign weighted = weighted | plus: part
    assign part = r3 | times: 3
    assign weighted = weighted | plus: part
    assign part = r2 | times: 2
    assign weighted = weighted | plus: part
    assign weighted = weighted | plus: r1
    assign review_average = weighted | times: 1.0 | divided_by: review_total | round: 1
  else
    comment
      no distribution anywhere: fall back to whatever a review app has written
      to the standard rating metafields, and draw no bars rather than invent any
    endcomment
    assign review_total = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | default: 0 | times: 1
    assign review_average = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating | default: 0 | times: 1.0 | round: 1
  endif

  assign show_reviews = false
  if section.settings.reviews_enabled and review_total > 0
    assign show_reviews = true
  endif

  comment
    The count is formatted once and joined to its label here, rather than being
    written next to a render tag where a whitespace-stripping delimiter was
    eating the space and printing "9,986reviews".
  endcomment
  capture review_count_number
    render 'number-comma', value: review_total
  endcapture
  assign review_count_number = review_count_number | strip
  assign review_count_label = review_count_number | append: ' Reviews'

  comment
    The product's own size guide, from the "Size guide image" metafield. Nothing
    is rendered at all when it is empty, so a product without one shows no link.
  endcomment
  assign size_guide = product.metafields.custom.size_guide_image.value
  if size_guide == blank
    assign size_guide = product.metafields.custom.size_guide.value
  endif

  assign media_groups = ''
  if color_option and product.media.size > 0
    assign color_position = color_option.position

    comment
      Every media item any variant points at, so a positional range can be
      stopped from claiming a shot that demonstrably belongs to another colour.
    endcomment
    capture variant_media_all
      for variant in product.variants
        if variant.featured_media
          echo '|'
          echo variant.featured_media.id
        endif
      endfor
      echo '|'
    endcapture

    comment
      Per colour, in colour order: the media its own variants point at, the
      first of those (IMG 1), and that one's position (the range anchor).
    endcomment
    capture colour_media_csv
      for value in color_option.values
        for variant in product.variants
          if color_position == 1
            assign variant_value = variant.option1
          elsif color_position == 2
            assign variant_value = variant.option2
          else
            assign variant_value = variant.option3
          endif
          comment
            option.values yields value drops, variant.optionN yields strings, so
            both sides are forced to a string before they are compared
          endcomment
          assign value_name = value | append: ''
          if variant_value == value_name and variant.featured_media
            echo '|'
            echo variant.featured_media.id
          endif
        endfor
        echo '|'
        unless forloop.last
          echo '~'
        endunless
      endfor
    endcapture
    assign colour_media = colour_media_csv | split: '~'

    capture primary_csv
      for value in color_option.values
        assign primary_id = 0
        assign primary_pos = 0
        for variant in product.variants
          if color_position == 1
            assign variant_value = variant.option1
          elsif color_position == 2
            assign variant_value = variant.option2
          else
            assign variant_value = variant.option3
          endif
          comment
            option.values yields value drops, variant.optionN yields strings, so
            both sides are forced to a string before they are compared
          endcomment
          assign value_name = value | append: ''
          if variant_value == value_name and variant.featured_media
            assign primary_id = variant.featured_media.id
            assign primary_pos = variant.featured_media.position
            break
          endif
        endfor
        echo primary_id
        echo ':'
        echo primary_pos
        unless forloop.last
          echo ','
        endunless
      endfor
    endcapture
    assign primaries = primary_csv | split: ','

    capture media_groups
      echo '{"option_index":'
      echo color_position | minus: 1
      echo ',"colors":{'
      for value in color_option.values
        assign pair = primaries[forloop.index0] | strip | split: ':'
        assign primary_id = pair[0] | times: 1
        assign anchor = pair[1] | times: 1
        assign mine = colour_media[forloop.index0]

        comment
          The range runs from this colour's anchor to the next colour's. Shots
          ahead of the very first anchor are deliberately left out: they belong
          to no variant, and folding them in is what used to put a generic
          product shot into IMG 1.
        endcomment
        assign stop = 99999
        for other in primaries
          assign other_pos = other | strip | split: ':' | last | times: 1
          if other_pos > anchor and other_pos < stop
            assign stop = other_pos
          endif
        endfor

        unless forloop.first
          echo ','
        endunless
        assign group_key = value | append: '' | downcase | strip
        echo group_key | json
        echo ':{"primary":'
        echo primary_id
        echo ',"media":['

        assign written = 0
        if primary_id > 0
          echo primary_id
          assign written = 1
        endif
        for media in product.media
          assign needle = '|' | append: media.id | append: '|'
          assign include = false
          if media.id == primary_id
            assign include = false
          elsif mine contains needle
            comment
              another of this colour's variants points at it, wherever it sits
            endcomment
            assign include = true
          elsif anchor > 0 and media.position > anchor and media.position < stop
            unless variant_media_all contains needle
              assign include = true
            endunless
          endif
          if include
            if written > 0
              echo ','
            endif
            echo media.id
            assign written = written | plus: 1
          endif
        endfor
        echo ']}'
      endfor
      echo '}}'
    endcapture
  endif

  assign po_base = settings.preorder_page_url | default: '/pages/special-order'
  capture preorder_href
    echo po_base
    echo '?product='
    echo po_product
    echo '&link='
    echo po_link
  endcapture
-%}

<div class="page-width">
  <div class="product-page" data-product-form-wrapper data-update-url data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}">
    <script type="application/json" data-product-json>{{ product | json }}</script>

    {%- if media_groups != blank -%}
      <script type="application/json" data-media-groups>{{ media_groups }}</script>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      assign slot_count = product.media.size
      if slot_count > 3
        assign slot_count = 3
      endif
      if slot_count < 1
        assign slot_count = 1
      endif
    -%}
    <div class="product-gallery" data-gallery-grid data-slots="{{ slot_count }}">
      {%- if product.media.size > 0 -%}
        {%- for media in product.media -%}
          <div
            class="product-gallery__item{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"
            data-gallery-item
            data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
            data-media-type="{{ media.media_type }}"
            {%- comment -%} the first three fill the desktop grid; mobile ignores the slot {%- endcomment -%}
            {% if forloop.index0 < 3 %}data-slot="{{ forloop.index0 }}"{% endif %}
          >
            {%- case media.media_type -%}
              {%- when 'image' -%}
                <img
                  src="{{ media | image_url: width: 1100 }}"
                  srcset="{{ media | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w, {{ media | image_url: width: 1100 }} 1100w, {{ media | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w"
                  sizes="(max-width: 899px) 86vw, 55vw"
                  alt="{{ media.alt | escape }}"
                  {% if forloop.first %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}
                  width="1100"
                  height="{{ 1100 | divided_by: media.aspect_ratio | round }}"
                >
              {%- when 'video', 'external_video' -%}
                {{ media | media_tag }}
              {%- else -%}
                {{ media | media_tag }}
            {%- endcase -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="product-gallery__item is-active" data-slot="0">{{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="product-info">
      {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          With three shots or fewer the desktop grid holds them all, so the
          carousel has nothing left to show there. Mobile still shows it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="product-thumbs-wrap"{% if product.media.size <= 3 %} data-thumbs-empty{% endif %}>
          <button type="button" class="product-thumbs__arrow product-thumbs__arrow--prev" data-thumbs-prev aria-label="Previous images">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="product-thumbs" data-thumbs-track>
          {%- for media in product.media -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="product-thumb{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"
              data-gallery-thumb
              data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
              {%- comment -%} already on the desktop grid, so kept out of the desktop carousel {%- endcomment -%}
              {% if forloop.index0 < 3 %}data-thumb-hidden{% endif %}
              aria-pressed="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
              aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} — {{ forloop.index }}"
            >
              <img src="{{ media | image_url: width: 220 }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="110" height="138">
            </button>
          {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="product-thumbs__arrow product-thumbs__arrow--next" data-thumbs-next aria-label="More images">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h1 class="product-info__title">{{ product.title | downcase }}</h1>
      <div class="product-info__price">
        <span data-price>{% render 'price', variant: product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}</span>
        <span class="preorder-badge">{{ settings.preorder_label | default: 'Pre-Order' }}</span>
        {%- if show_reviews -%}
          {%- comment -%} reads as text next to the price, not as a control {%- endcomment -%}
          <a class="pdp-rating" href="#customer-reviews" data-scroll-to-reviews>
            {% render 'rating-stars', rating: review_average, size: 12 %}
            <span class="pdp-rating__score">{{ review_average }}</span>
            <span class="pdp-rating__separator" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
            <span class="pdp-rating__count">{{ review_count_label }}</span>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- form 'product', product, data-ajax-add: '' -%}
        {%- liquid
          comment
            Nothing is selected on arrival: the customer picks the options
            themselves. A ?variant= link is an explicit choice, so that one is
            honoured, and a product with no options has nothing to choose.
          endcomment
          assign current_variant = product.selected_variant
          assign needs_options = false
          if product.has_only_default_variant
            assign current_variant = product.variants.first
          elsif current_variant == nil
            assign needs_options = true
          endif
        -%}

        {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
          {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
            {%- comment -%} the colour option is the one already resolved above {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign is_color_option = false -%}
            {%- if color_option and option.position == color_option.position -%}
              {%- assign is_color_option = true -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            <fieldset class="option-group" data-option-group style="border: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 20px;">
              {%- assign option_name_lower = option.name | downcase -%}
              <legend class="option-group__label">
                {{ option_name_lower }}
                {%- if size_guide and option_name_lower contains 'size' -%}
                  <button type="button" class="size-guide-link" data-size-guide-open aria-haspopup="dialog">
                    {{ 'products.product.size_guide' | t: default: 'size guide' }}
                  </button>
                {%- endif -%}
              </legend>
              <div class="option-pills">
                {%- for value in option.values -%}
                  <span class="option-pill">
                    <input
                      type="radio"
                      id="Option-{{ section.id }}-{{ option.position }}-{{ forloop.index }}"
                      name="option-{{ option.position }}"
                      value="{{ value | escape }}"
                      {% if current_variant and option.selected_value == value %}checked{% endif %}
                    >
                    <label for="Option-{{ section.id }}-{{ option.position }}-{{ forloop.index }}">
                      {%- if is_color_option -%}{% render 'option-swatch', value: value %}{%- endif -%}
                      {{ value | downcase }}
                    </label>
                  </span>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </fieldset>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endunless -%}

        <div class="option-group">
          <p class="option-group__label">{{ 'products.product.quantity' | t }}</p>
          <div class="qty-input">
            <button type="button" data-qty-change="-1" aria-label="decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
            <input type="number" name="quantity" value="1" min="1" aria-label="{{ 'products.product.quantity' | t }}">
            <button type="button" data-qty-change="1" aria-label="increase quantity">+</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} empty until the customer has chosen, so no variant is assumed {%- endcomment -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current_variant.id }}">

        {%- if settings.preorder_message != blank -%}
          <p class="preorder-note">{{ settings.preorder_message }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="product-form__buttons" data-buy-observe>
          <button
            type="submit"
            class="btn btn--solid btn--full"
            data-add-to-cart
            data-label-add="{{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}"
            data-label-choose="{{ 'products.product.choose_options' | t }}"
            {%- comment -%}
              data-needs-options is what separates "has not chosen yet" from
              "chose something that cannot be bought": both disable the button,
              but only the second one brings out the pre-order CTA.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {% if needs_options %}data-needs-options{% endif %}
            {% if needs_options or current_variant.available == false %}disabled{% endif %}
          >
            <span data-add-to-cart-text>
              {%- if needs_options -%}
                {{ 'products.product.choose_options' | t }}
              {%- elsif current_variant.available -%}
                {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
              {%- else -%}
                {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
          </button>
          {{ form | payment_button }}

          {%- comment -%} replaces the buy buttons whenever the chosen variant is unavailable {%- endcomment -%}
          <a class="preorder-cta" href="{{ preorder_href }}">
            <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            {{ settings.preorder_cta_label | default: 'Create an order request' }}
          </a>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          A sibling of the buttons, not a child: the pre-order swap hides what is
          inside that container, and the row belongs under it either way.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'payment-icons', class: 'payment-icons--product' %}
      {%- endform -%}

      <div class="product-accordions">
        {%- if product.description != blank -%}
          <details>
            <summary>{{ 'products.product.description' | t }}</summary>
            <div class="accordion__content rte">{{ product.description }}</div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == 'accordion' and block.settings.content != blank -%}
            <details {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <summary>{{ block.settings.title | downcase }}</summary>
              <div class="accordion__content">{{ block.settings.content }}</div>
            </details>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- if show_reviews -%}
  <section class="page-width reviews" id="customer-reviews" aria-labelledby="customer-reviews-title">
    <h2 class="reviews__title" id="customer-reviews-title">{{ 'products.product.customer_reviews' | t: default: 'Customer Reviews' }}</h2>

    <div class="reviews__overview">
      <div class="reviews__score">
        <span class="reviews__average">{{ review_average }}</span>
        {%- assign rating_label = review_average | append: ' out of 5 stars' -%}
        {% render 'rating-stars', rating: review_average, size: 17, label: rating_label %}
        <span class="reviews__total">{{ review_count_label }}</span>
      </div>

      {%- if has_distribution -%}
        <ol class="reviews__bars">
          {%- for level in (1..5) -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign star = 6 | minus: level
              case star
                when 5
                  assign bucket = r5
                when 4
                  assign bucket = r4
                when 3
                  assign bucket = r3
                when 2
                  assign bucket = r2
                else
                  assign bucket = r1
              endcase
              assign share = bucket | times: 100.0 | divided_by: review_total
            -%}
            <li class="reviews__bar">
              <span class="reviews__bar-stars">
                {{ star }}
                {% render 'icon-star', class: 'reviews__bar-star' %}
              </span>
              <span class="reviews__track"><span class="reviews__fill" style="width: {{ share }}%;"></span></span>
              <span class="reviews__bar-count">{% render 'number-comma', value: bucket %}</span>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ol>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if review_fit_label != blank -%}
        <div class="reviews__fit">
          <h3 class="reviews__subtitle">{{ section.settings.fit_heading | default: 'How does it fit?' }}</h3>
          <p class="reviews__fit-result">{{ review_fit_label }}</p>
          <div class="fit-scale" style="--fit: {{ review_fit_position }}%;">
            <span class="fit-scale__line" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- for tick in (1..5) -%}<span class="fit-scale__tick"></span>{%- endfor -%}
            </span>
            <span class="fit-scale__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <p class="fit-scale__ends">
            <span>{{ section.settings.fit_min_label | default: 'Small' }}</span>
            <span>{{ section.settings.fit_max_label | default: 'Big' }}</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if review_summary_text != blank or review_keywords_text != blank -%}
      <div class="reviews__detail">
        {%- if review_summary_text != blank -%}
          <article class="review-summary">
            <h3 class="review-summary__title">
              <svg class="review-summary__spark" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 0l1.5 4.6L14 6l-4.5 1.4L8 12 6.5 7.4 2 6l4.5-1.4z"/><path d="M13.2 10.4l.6 1.8 1.8.6-1.8.6-.6 1.8-.6-1.8-1.8-.6 1.8-.6z"/></svg>
              {{ section.settings.summary_heading | default: 'Review Summary' }}
            </h3>
            <p class="review-summary__meta">
              {{ 'products.product.summary_meta' | t: default: 'Based on' }} {{ review_count_number }} customer reviews
            </p>
            <p class="review-summary__body">{{ review_summary_text }}</p>
          </article>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if review_keywords_text != blank -%}
          <div class="reviews__mentions">
            <h3 class="reviews__subtitle">{{ section.settings.keywords_heading | default: 'What customers mention' }}</h3>
            <ul class="reviews__tags">
              {%- assign keyword_lines = review_keywords_text | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
              {%- for line in keyword_lines -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign entry = line | strip
                  if entry == blank
                    continue
                  endif
                  assign parts = entry | split: '|'
                  assign keyword_label = parts[0] | strip
                  assign keyword_count = parts[1] | strip
                -%}
                <li class="reviews__tag">
                  {{ keyword_label }}
                  {%- if keyword_count != blank -%}
                    <span class="reviews__tag-count">{% render 'number-comma', value: keyword_count %}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if size_guide -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The image at its own size, capped at three quarters of the viewport. The
    dialog shrink-wraps it, so there is no empty box around a chart that does
    not happen to be 3:4.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="size-guide" data-size-guide hidden>
    <div class="size-guide__scrim" data-size-guide-close></div>
    <div
      class="size-guide__dialog"
      role="dialog"
      aria-modal="true"
      aria-label="{{ 'products.product.size_guide' | t: default: 'Size guide' }}"
    >
      <button
        type="button"
        class="size-guide__close"
        data-size-guide-close
        aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.close' | t: default: 'Close' }}"
      >
        {% render 'icon', name: 'close' %}
      </button>
      <img
        class="size-guide__image"
        src="{{ size_guide | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
        srcset="{{ size_guide | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ size_guide | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w, {{ size_guide | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w"
        sizes="75vw"
        alt="{{ size_guide.alt | default: 'Size guide' | escape }}"
        width="{{ size_guide.width | default: 1600 }}"
        height="{{ size_guide.height | default: 900 }}"
        loading="lazy"
      >
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Shown once the buy controls leave the viewport. Pointer events are off in the
  stylesheet so the bar never takes a click meant for the page underneath it;
  the + button turns them back on for itself. It opens the cart drawer's own
  mini PDP rather than carrying a second buy button.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="pdp-bar" data-pdp-bar>
  <span class="pdp-bar__media">
    {%- if product.featured_media -%}
      <img
        data-pdp-bar-image
        src="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 160 }}"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
        width="80"
        height="107"
      >
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>
  <span class="pdp-bar__title">{{ product.title | downcase }}</span>
  <span class="pdp-bar__price" data-pdp-bar-price>
    {%- render 'price', variant: product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
  </span>
  <button
    type="button"
    class="pdp-bar__add"
    data-pdp-bar-add
    aria-label="{{ 'products.product.choose_options' | t }} — {{ product.title | escape }}"
  >
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5.5v13M5.5 12h13"/></svg>
  </button>
</div>

<div style="height: clamp(40px, 6vw, 88px);"></div>

